sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant K as YubiKey
    participant B as Browser
    participant G as Gateway worker
    participant M as MySQL

    B->>G: Start login with username and account password
    G->>M: Open connection and authenticate password factor 1
    activate M
    M-->>G: Fresh WebAuthn factor-2 challenge
    G->>M: Credential-ID request
    M-->>G: AuthMoreData - credential ID or empty response
    G-->>B: WebAuthn get options through the owner-bound flow
    Note over B,G: Use allowCredentials when an ID is present or discover otherwise
    B->>K: Request assertion - touch, and verification if required
    K-->>B: Signed assertion
    Note over K,B: Private key and PIN stay local
    B->>G: Serialized assertion and one-use request_id
    G->>G: Check origin, challenge, RP hash and user presence
    G->>M: Encoded assertion with original signed client data

    alt MySQL accepts the authentication
        M-->>G: Authentication OK
        Note over G,M: Normal session setup is now allowed
        G->>M: SELECT 'hello world', CURRENT_USER(), CONNECTION_ID(), @@version
        M-->>G: Query result under the authenticated account
        G->>M: Close the user's connection
        G-->>B: Success and query result
    else MySQL rejects the authentication
        M-->>G: Authentication error
        G->>M: Close the failed connection
        G-->>B: Error event - no proof query
    end
    deactivate M
